{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774718,"nonce":"DRGvZJZHZVNsUL5+nS0X8kqSXFI=","title":"Reconcile ADR statuses with reality; wire the New-environment dialog","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #32 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/reconcile-adr-status-and-env-dialog` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-18T19:43:47Z · Merged: 2026-07-18T19:44:55Z\n\n\nWhile answering \"is ADR-0037 actually implemented?\" a codebase audit (@ `main`) found the docs and UI had drifted from what's actually shipped. This PR reconciles both. ADR-0037 (and 0038/0039/0041/0042/0045–0054) **are** implemented on `main`; the only genuine gap in the whole ADR set is ADR-0015's attestation/provenance half (left as-is here).\n\n\n**`docs(adr)` — mark 0045–0054 Accepted**\nThese ten ADRs were still labelled `Proposed` in both the individual files and the README index despite all being implemented on `main` (clone step, forge adapters, retry/dead-letter, fail-closed startup, RBAC, retention GC, multi-replica, artifacts, observability, embedded UI + run cancel). \"Proposed\" here just meant nobody bumped the status after landing.\n\n**`fix(web-ui)` — de-facade the New-environment dialog + fix stale copy**\nADR-0037's environments API (`PUT /v1/repos/{org}/{repo}/environments/{name}`) has shipped, but the UI still carried pre-landing facades:\n- The **New-environment dialog** was a non-functional stub — decorative controls, a Create button that only closed the modal, and a note claiming it \"Persists once the environments backend lands (ADR-0037)\". Now wired for real: new `putEnvironment()` client fn + form controls mapping 1:1 onto `ProtectionRules` (approvers / wait_timer / allowed_refs / concurrency), saving/error states, and an `envEpoch` refetch so a created environment appears immediately.\n- The **RepoView header comment** still described removed branch/trigger filters as present. Corrected to record that the Runs list carries only a status filter today, and that restoring branch/PR filters is backend-first (needs `RunSummaryDto` to expose branch/trigger/PR).\n\n- `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` green.\n- Request contract confirmed against the server handler (`put_environment` takes `Json\u003cProtectionRules\u003e`).\n- **Not yet done:** a live end-to-end click-through of the create flow (needs the local stack up + Administer auth). Happy to follow up with a `just`-driven live run.\n\n- Restore branch/PR filters on the Runs list once `RunSummaryDto` carries provenance.\n- Sweep for any other leftover \"post-ADR-XXXX / not yet\" facades in the UI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}